Clips Kitty Editor
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The Editor page shows Clips Kitty Editor, a separate program kept in its own
repository (https://github.com/ColinGPT9/clips-kitty-editor). It is based on
Concat (https://github.com/jub0t/Concat), Copyright its authors, and is
licensed under the GNU Affero General Public License, version 3 or later
(AGPL-3.0-or-later), the licence Concat is published under. Concat's name is
used only to say what the editor is based on; Clips Kitty Editor is a
modified build and is not Concat. What it changes, and why, is listed in
PATCHES.md at the top of its repository, with its complete source.

Its folder carries its own LICENSE and THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md, which travel
with it wherever it is shipped. In short, it includes:

  FFmpeg libraries          LGPL         decoding, encoding and muxing in the
                                         editor: BtbN's lgpl-shared build of
                                         FFmpeg 8.1 for Windows
                                         (LGPL-3.0-or-later), as DLLs beside
                                         the program, with nothing GPL-only or
                                         non-free in it. Source:
                                         https://ffmpeg.org/download.html
  Slint                     GPL-3.0-only its interface toolkit, used under the
                                         GPL
  whisper.cpp and ggml      MIT          the editor's own captions from speech
  ONNX Runtime              MIT          the editor's sound and picture models
  Microsoft Visual C++      Microsoft    runtime DLLs beside the program
  runtime                   terms
  Hanken Grotesk and its    see its      the editor's caption and title fonts
  other fonts               notices

The models, voices and sounds the editor can download are not bundled; each
is fetched only when a person asks for it there, and its licence is named in
the editor's THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.


